\b CoreLMS \u8212? World-Class Project Plan (Roadmap + Checklist)\b0\par
\par
\b How to use this document\b0\par
1) Work in phases (P0..P6).\par
2) Each phase has: goals, checklist, and Definition of Done (DoD).\par
3) Only start the next phase when the current DoD is satisfied.\par
\par
\b Project Context (current stack)\b0\par
\bullet\tab Frontend: Next.js (App Router), React, TypeScript, Tailwind, react-markdown.\par
\bullet\tab Backend: FastAPI, SQLAlchemy/Alembic, Redis, RQ workers.\par
\bullet\tab Infra: Docker Compose, Nginx (local), Caddy (TLS profile), Postgres, S3-compatible storage.\par
\par
\b Guiding Principles (world-class)\b0\par
\bullet\tab Security by default (least privilege, secrets hygiene, hardened cookies, safe headers).\par
\bullet\tab Reliability first (clear failure modes, retries, idempotency, health/readiness, observability).\par
\bullet\tab Great UX (consistent typography/layout, accessibility, fast perceived performance).\par
\bullet\tab Developer Experience (repeatable envs, CI, tests, lint/typecheck, fast feedback).\par
\bullet\tab Operability (easy deploy, rollbacks, monitoring, backups, incident playbooks).\par
\par
\b Quality Gates (must always pass)\b0\par
\bullet\tab Frontend: build succeeds; lint/typecheck clean or explicitly waived with rationale.\par
\bullet\tab Backend: migrations OK; health endpoints OK; structured errors with request_id.\par
\bullet\tab Security: no secrets in git; no large binaries in git; dependency scanning enabled.\par
\bullet\tab Regression safety: smoke tests for auth + critical flows.\par
\par
\b Phase P0 \u8212? Repo Hygiene + Safety Rails (1 day)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Prevent accidental commits of secrets/binaries; standardize repo tooling.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
[ ] Ensure .env is in .gitignore and never committed.\par
[ ] Add guards for large files (>20MB) via pre-commit + CI (reject).\par
[ ] Add secret scanning: gitleaks (CI) + local optional hook.\par
[ ] Add editorconfig (line endings, indentation) to reduce CRLF/LF churn.\par
[ ] Add CONTRIBUTING workflow: how to run, test, lint, build, deploy.\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab No secrets in git history on main; CI fails if secrets/big files appear.\par
\bullet\tab A new dev can clone and run with documented steps.\par
\par
\b Phase P1 \u8212? Environments + Configuration Excellence (1\u8211?2 days)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Make local/VPS/prod configs explicit, safe, and predictable.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
[ ] Split env templates: .env.example (safe placeholders) + optional .env.local/.env.vps docs.\par
[ ] Hard requirement: strong JWT secret in prod (fail-fast already exists).\par
[ ] Cookie settings matrix: secure, domain, sameSite; validate per environment.\par
[ ] CORS allowlist correctness per PUBLIC_APP_URL.\par
[ ] Proxy trust: TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=true only behind trusted proxies; keep TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS accurate.\par
[ ] Document routing: Nginx/Caddy \u8594? Next \u8594? /api/backend/* \u8594? FastAPI.\par
[ ] Add a single command for full rebuild (compose profiles).\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab Running the app on local/VPS/prod is a cookbook (no guessing).\par
\bullet\tab A misconfigured env fails loudly with clear errors.\par
\par
\b Phase P2 \u8212? Security Hardening (2\u8211?4 days)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Treat project like fintech: robust sessions, secure defaults, auditability.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
\b 2.1 Authentication & Sessions\b0\par
[ ] Refresh token rotation tested (race conditions handled).\par
[ ] Session store (Redis) supports: list sessions, revoke one, revoke all, idle/absolute timeouts.\par
[ ] Rate limits on auth endpoints (login/refresh/password change).\par
[ ] Optional device fingerprint (non-invasive): UA hash + IP prefix policy; document tradeoffs.\par
\b 2.2 Transport & Headers\b0\par
[ ] HSTS in prod verified only when TLS is enabled.\par
[ ] Add Content-Security-Policy appropriate for Next + API.\par
[ ] Ensure cookies are HttpOnly, Secure (prod), SameSite policy defined.\par
\b 2.3 Dependency & SAST\b0\par
[ ] Dependabot (or Renovate) enabled.\par
[ ] Python: pip-audit; JS: npm/yarn audit in CI (or Snyk).\par
[ ] Basic SAST (semgrep) rules for FastAPI/JS.\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab Security checklist passes; critical vulnerabilities addressed or explicitly accepted.\par
\bullet\tab Attack surface documented (auth, uploads, streaming, admin).\par
\par
\b Phase P3 \u8212? Reliability + Observability (2\u8211?5 days)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Make failures diagnosable; ensure background jobs are resilient.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
\b 3.1 Logging\b0\par
[ ] Structured logs everywhere (rid, user_id, ip, path, duration_ms, status).\par
[ ] PII policy: never log tokens/passwords; scrub headers.\par
\b 3.2 Metrics & Tracing\b0\par
[ ] Prometheus metrics endpoint (latency, errors, rq queue depth).\par
[ ] Optional OpenTelemetry traces (start with HTTP + DB spans).\par
\b 3.3 Background Jobs (RQ)\b0\par
[ ] Retry/backoff strategy per job type; idempotency keys where possible.\par
[ ] Dead-letter / failed job inspection process.\par
[ ] Job timeouts and max runtime budgets documented.\par
\b 3.4 Health/Readiness\b0\par
[ ] /health/ready checks DB + Redis; S3 optionally.\par
[ ] Docker healthchecks align with real readiness.\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab When something breaks, you can answer: what failed, where, for which user, and why.\par
\par
\b Phase P4 \u8212? World-Class UX/UI (3\u8211?7 days)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Make lessons and dashboard feel premium: typography, spacing, accessibility.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
\b 4.1 Design System\b0\par
[ ] Define tokens: spacing scale, font scale, colors, radii, shadows.\par
[ ] Standard components: Button, Card, Modal, Form fields, Toasts, Empty states.\par
[ ] A11y: focus styles, keyboard navigation, aria labels.\par
\b 4.2 Lesson Rendering\b0\par
[ ] Robust Markdown normalization (handles sloppy pasted content).\par
[ ] \u8220?Section cards\u8221? mode: numbered sections as cards (badge + title + body).\par
[ ] Typography: consistent margins, line-height, max width; avoid orphan headings.\par
[ ] Media: images/video/pdf preview with safe sandboxing; responsive behavior.\par
\b 4.3 Voice-over UX\b0\par
[ ] Two-voice selection (male/female) compact in header controls.\par
[ ] Rate/pitch controls persisted; pause/resume stable across browsers.\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab A new user instantly feels the product is premium and consistent.\par
\par
\b Phase P5 \u8212? Performance (1\u8211?3 days)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Keep app fast on slow networks and mid devices.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
[ ] Measure: Lighthouse + Web Vitals baseline.\par
[ ] Code splitting: avoid importing heavy components on initial route.\par
[ ] API caching strategy (where safe): ETags, cache headers for static assets.\par
[ ] S3 streaming endpoints support Range (quickstart already does) + correct cache headers.\par
[ ] DB: add indexes for hot queries; analyze slow queries.\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab Median page loads are fast; no obvious long tasks; server handles spikes gracefully.\par
\par
\b Phase P6 \u8212? Testing + CI/CD (3\u8211?7 days)\b0\par
\b Goals\b0\par
\bullet\tab Make regressions rare; make deployments safe and repeatable.\par
\b Checklist\b0\par
\b 6.1 Backend Tests (pytest)\b0\par
[ ] Auth flows: login/refresh/logout; session listing/revocation.\par
[ ] Proxy/IP extraction tests (trusted vs untrusted).\par
[ ] Quickstart streaming tests incl. Range headers (206/416).\par
[ ] Storage presign/upload flows; permission checks.\par
\b 6.2 Frontend Tests\b0\par
[ ] Playwright smoke: login, dashboard, open lesson, quickstart playback, refresh token path.\par
\b 6.3 CI\b0\par
[ ] Lint + typecheck + tests + docker build in CI.\par
[ ] Secret scan + dependency scan in CI.\par
\b 6.4 Deployment\b0\par
[ ] Deploy runbook: backup DB, pull, migrate, health check, rollback steps.\par
[ ] Backups: DB dumps, S3 lifecycle, retention policy.\par
\b Definition of Done\b0\par
\bullet\tab Every merge is validated by CI; deployments are routine with rollback.\par
\par
\b Execution Schedule (recommended)\b0\par
\bullet\tab Week 1: P0\u8594?P2 (hygiene, env, security).\par
\bullet\tab Week 2: P3\u8594?P4 (observability, UX).\par
\bullet\tab Week 3: P5\u8594?P6 (performance, testing, CI/CD).\par
\par
\b Appendix A: Required Docs (deliverables)\b0\par
[ ] README: local run, docker profiles, troubleshooting.\par
[ ] VPS runbook: env setup, domain+TLS, rebuild, migrations, verification checklist.\par
[ ] Security.md updated: threat model, secrets handling, contact.\par
[ ] Architecture.md: diagrams and request routing.\par
\par
\b Appendix B: Quick Wins (do anytime)\b0\par
[ ] Add pre-commit: formatters + gitleaks + big file blocker.\par
[ ] Add \u8220?make-like\u8221? scripts: dev, build, test, lint, migrate.\par
[ ] Add admin safety confirmations for destructive operations.\par
